==Welsh==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|cy|myned}} {{qualifier|literary}}

===Etymology===
Suppletive verb; verbal noun from {{inh|cy|wlm|mynet}}, from {{inh|cy|cel-bry-pro|*monetu}} (compare {{cog|kw|mones}}, {{cog|br|mont}}), verbal noun of {{inh|cy|cel-pro|*mon-ī-}} (compare {{cog|mga|muinithir||goes around}}), from {{inh|cy|ine-pro|*menH-}} (compare {{cog|xum|menes||will come}}, {{cog|lt|mìnti||to trample, scutch}}). Indicative forms from {{der|cy|cel-pro|*ago-||to drive}} (compare {{cog|sga|aigid}}), from {{der|cy|ine-pro|*h₂eǵ-}} (compare {{cog|la|agō}}). The forms in ''el-'' are from {{der|cy|cel-pro|*ɸel-||to approach, drive}}, from {{der|cy|ine-pro|*pelh₂-}} (compare {{cog|la|pellō||strike, drive}}, Epic Greek {{m|grc|πίλναμαι||approach}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|cy-N}} {{IPA|/mɨ̞nd/|lang=cy}}
* {{a|cy-S}} {{IPA|/mɪnd/|lang=cy}}

===Verb===
{{head|cy|verb|irregular|cat2=irregular verbs}}

# to [[go]]
#: {{ux|cy|Mae hi'n '''mynd''' i Gaerdydd heno.|inline=1|t=She's going to Cardiff tonight.}}
#: {{ux|cy|'''Aeth''' hi ddoe.|inline=1|t=She went yesterday.}}
#: {{ux|cy|'''Awn''' ni ac yn edrych.|inline=1|t=We will go and look.}}
#: {{ux|cy|'''Aet''' ti i'r ysgol ar droed.|inline=1|t=You went/used to go to school on foot.}}
#: {{ux|cy|Mae'n angenrheidiol yr '''elwyf''' nawr.|inline=1|t=It is necessary that I go now.}}
#: {{ux|cy|Na, rwy'n '''mynd''' ar y trên bach.|t=No, I'm taking the little train.|inline=1}}

